        "kind": "statements",
        "evidence_id": "E-ab863beddb4ab0a2517976fa",
        "quote": "The LUCI project achieved the first-ever, extended duration combustion tests (greater than 25 seconds) in simulated \nLunar gravity.  The results are applicable to NASA’s exploration efforts in that they guide the selection of fire-safe \nmaterials and environments and ensure safety of future spacecraft and Lunar habitats.  The data also provides \nfundamental understanding of fires burning at reduced gravity for comparison to sophisticated numerical models.  \nFinally, the experiment is a steppingstone to the ultimate goal of performing burn tests on the Lunar surface in the \nFlammability of Materials on the Moon (FM2) experiment which will fly on a SpaceX Human Lander System \nunmanned test flight. \n",
